e 21st coolest November 13 high (tied) of 113 since 1911, the coolest since 2019. The normal high for the date is 80\u00b0F, and the record is 92\u00b0F (1972). The low of <strong>65\u00b0F</strong> was the 23rd warmest November 13 low (tied) of 114 since 1911.","t_rec":"Sarasota-Bradenton has nearly stopped setting record lows","p_rec":"If Sarasota-Bradenton's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Sarasota-Bradenton has set <strong class=\"sig\">9 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 86 that chance alone would give, and <strong>104 record highs</strong>, close to the 85 that chance alone would give. The 1990s hold the most record highs of any decade (80). Sarasota-Bradenton's all-time high is 101\u00b0F, on July 23, 1971.","t_chg":"Sarasota-Bradenton's days and nights both warmed. Nights warmed faster.","p_chg":"Across 107 complete years: Sarasota-Bradenton's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.38\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.30 to +0.47), about +4.3\u00b0F since 1911. Sarasota-Bradenton's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.09\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.02 to +0.15), about +1.0\u00b0F since 1911.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 11 of 12 months. Highs rose in 4 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Sarasota-Bradenton's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.30 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 50.2 inches a year. The wettest year was 1957 (82.98 in); the driest, 2023 (27.13 in). Sarasota-Bradenton almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 0.0 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 6 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}